From: Piotr Kubik <piotr.kubik@adtran.com>
Date: Tue, 13 May 2026
Subject: [PATCH] net: ethernet: mediatek: limit GRO aggregation on 2500base-x ports

On devices using 2500base-x SerDes with PHY rate adaptation 
the default 64K GRO aggregation size causes throughput degradation when
bridging to a port linked at a lower speed (e.g. 1G).

Reduce gro_max_size to 32K on 2500base-x ports.

Signed-off-by: Piotr Kubik <piotr.kubik@adtran.com>
---
 drivers/net/ethernet/mediatek/mtk_eth_soc.c | 10 ++++++++++
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+)

--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/mediatek/mtk_eth_soc.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/mediatek/mtk_eth_soc.c
@@ -5459,6 +5459,16 @@ static int mtk_add_mac(struct mtk_eth *e
 	eth->netdev[id]->features |= eth->soc->hw_features;
 	eth->netdev[id]->ethtool_ops = &mtk_ethtool_ops;
 
+	/* Limit GRO aggregation size on 2500base-x ports. The default 64K
+	 * causes throughput degradation when bridging to a lower-speed port
+	 * due to burst overflows at the PHY rate adaptation boundary
+	 * (2500base-x SerDes -> SGMII at 1G copper).
+	 */
+	if (phy_mode == PHY_INTERFACE_MODE_2500BASEX) {
+		WRITE_ONCE(eth->netdev[id]->gro_max_size, SZ_32K);
+		WRITE_ONCE(eth->netdev[id]->gro_ipv4_max_size, SZ_32K);
+	}
+
 	eth->netdev[id]->irq = eth->irq[0];
 	eth->netdev[id]->dev.of_node = np;
 
